  2. You'll see this message:
  ⏰ Staking points distribution scheduled (every 5 minutes for TESTING)

  3. Stake an NFT and sync
  4. Wait and watch the logs - Every 5 minutes you'll see:
  [Cron] Running staking points distribution...
  [Daily Points] Starting daily points distribution at 2024-01-01T12:05:00.000Z
  [Daily Points] Found X active staking records
  [Daily Points] Awarded Y points to 0x1234... (2 NFTs staked)
  [Cron] Distribution completed: { success: true, processed: 1, totalPointsDistributed: Y }

  Option 2: Manual Trigger (Instant Testing) ⚡

  Don't want to wait 5 minutes? Use the manual endpoint:

  # Trigger distribution immediately
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/staking/distribute-points

  Response:
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Distributed 5 points to 1 wallets",
    "data": {
      "success": true,
      "processed": 1,
      "totalPointsDistributed": 5,
      "timestamp": "2024-01-01T12:00:00.000Z"
    }
  }

  📋 Full Testing Flow:

  # 1. Start MongoDB (if not running)
  # mongod or Docker: docker run -d -p 27017:27017 mongo

  # 2. Start your server
  cd server
  npm start

  # 3. Stake an NFT (use your frontend or contract directly)

  # 4. Sync the staking state
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/staking/sync/0xYOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS

  # 5. Check initial state (should show 0 points)
  curl http://localhost:3001/api/staking/info/0xYOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS

  # 6. Wait 15 minutes OR trigger manually:
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/staking/distribute-points

  # 7. Check again (should show points awarded)
  curl http://localhost:3001/api/staking/info/0xYOUR_WALLET_ADDRESS

  🎯 Quick Test (Under 1 Minute):

  # 1. Start server
  npm start

  # 2. Stake NFT and sync
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/staking/sync/0xYOUR_WALLET

  # 3. Wait 30 seconds (so some time passes)

  # 4. Manually trigger distribution
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/staking/distribute-points

  # 5. Check points awarded
  curl http://localhost:3001/api/staking/info/0xYOUR_WALLET

  💡 Note About Vercel:

  When you do deploy to Vercel, standard cron jobs don't work on serverless platforms. You'll need to:

  Option A: Use Vercel Cron Jobs
  - Add a cron config in vercel.json
  - Call your distribution endpoint on schedule

  Option B: Use external cron service
  - Use services like cron-job.org or EasyCron
  - Hit your /api/staking/distribute-points endpoint daily

  But for now, local testing works perfectly! Just start your server. 🚀

